  "summary": "code16/sharp: Arbitrary class instantiation through the embed_key API parameter",
  "details": "### Impact\n\nAn authenticated attacker can instantiate any class in the PHP application by using the `embed_key` parameter across multiple API endpoints. The instantiation is performed by the Laravel container. As a result, the `__construct()` method of the class is called and all constructor dependencies are resolved. The attacker cannot specify parameter values and cannot call any arbitrary method.\n\n### Patches\n\nThe problem has been patched in 9.23.0 and pre-release version 10.0.0-beta.4. An additional check was added to verify that `embed_key` is a class extending `SharpFormEditorEmbed` before any instantiation.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nNo known workarounds.",
